@trait {
  name: "@temporal_guard",
  category: "devops",
  description: "Temporal logic guard that validates clock consistency and enforces time-window contracts on node events and state transitions. mode selects the enforcement posture: strict rejects any event or state transition whose timestamp falls outside the configured drift and future/past windows, emitting on_violation; relaxed permits minor drift violations but logs them as warnings via on_warning without blocking; permissive allows all timestamps through but still emits diagnostics so callers can observe drift without enforcement. max_clock_drift_ms is the maximum tolerable absolute difference in milliseconds between the node's local clock and the reference clock source before a violation is declared; set to 0 to disable drift checking. allowed_future_ms is the maximum number of milliseconds into the future an event timestamp may be relative to the current reference time — timestamps further ahead than this ceiling are treated as violations. allowed_past_ms is the maximum number of milliseconds into the past an event timestamp may be relative to the current reference time — timestamps older than this floor are treated as violations. clock_source selects the reference time provider: system uses the host OS clock (process.hrtime or Date.now); ntp queries a configured NTP pool and caches the offset; gps reads PPS or NMEA time from a connected GPS receiver (Jetson-compatible); holoscript defers to the HoloScript simulation clock for deterministic replay scenarios. on_violation fires when strict mode blocks an event — payload carries guardId, timestamp, drift_ms, and reason; on_warning fires in relaxed mode for the same conditions but without blocking; on_sync fires after a successful reference clock synchronisation. Research: TemporalGuardTrait.ts — guard lifecycle (tg:assert, tg:satisfy, tg:check), violation counter, deadline tracking via Map<guardId, {deadline, property}>.",
  props: {
    mode: enum("strict" | "relaxed" | "permissive") = "strict",
    max_clock_drift_ms: number = 500,
    allowed_future_ms: number = 1000,
    allowed_past_ms: number = 5000,
    clock_source: enum("system" | "ntp" | "gps" | "holoscript") = "system"
  },
  events: {
    attached: "temporal_guard:attached",
    detached: "temporal_guard:detached",
    on_violation: "temporal_guard:violation",
    on_warning: "temporal_guard:warning",
    on_sync: "temporal_guard:sync",
    on_assert: "temporal_guard:assert",
    on_satisfy: "temporal_guard:satisfy",
    on_check: "temporal_guard:check",
    on_set_mode: "temporal_guard:set_mode",
    on_set_clock_source: "temporal_guard:set_clock_source"
  },
  behaviors: ["@timeout_guard"]
}
